  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "PU1lvF87nwBbu2bjsFp7wLq5hUkd0om/lXDq6ENBsLrQNy2jmiz9HbjsbXsksVXAu1Y3bgT19knZjHJtAJi3Bw==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 38626,
  "published": "2026-07-23T08:09:39.037Z",
  "releaseNotes": "2.0.0 — transport is now config-selectable via `Messaging:Wolverine:Transport` = Postgres | RabbitMq | AzureServiceBus (default Postgres, back-compat with the flat connection-string config). Adds RabbitMQ + Azure Service Bus transports (native fan-out). Same consume-side behavioural contract on all three (ack-after-handler-success, bounded retry then dead-letter, immediate poison dead-lettering). Produce-side differs by transport: RabbitMq enables publisher confirmations so a reachable-but-rejecting broker is detected by Wolverine's sending agent — but note Wolverine never surfaces a sending failure to the ProduceAsync caller (it handles them via SendingFailure policies, default retry-then-discard), so on the brokered transports a produce drop is NOT caller-observable and the app-level outbox cannot detect it; true sender-side no-loss needs Wolverine's durable outbox (not wired here). Also, the publish-before-a-consumer-binds window stays open (Wolverine publishes mandatory:false), so consumer topology must be provisioned before producers publish. See MESSAGING-TRANSPORTS.md §4.4.",
